Reliable material recovery requires established relationships with specialized recyclers possessing appropriate equipment and expertise. Certified partnerships ensure material is actually recovered rather than exported to substandard facilities. Long-term partnership stability enables recycler investment in equipment and processes optimizing recovery from specific product streams.

Recycler partnerships create feedback mechanisms where processing challenges inform product design improvements. Transparent relationships build accountability preventing material laundering or export to environmentally damaging facilities. Partnerships enable manufacturers to verify EPR compliance and material recovery claims.